{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"agent_message","text":"I submitted the mitigation, and the endpoint accepted it as the mitigation stage.\n\n**Root cause:** The `product-catalog` pod was failing every database query with `password authentication failed for user \"otelu\"`. The `product-catalog-db-conn` secret and the PostgreSQL role both carry the correct password, and the Service and endpoints are correct. The running pod was holding stale credentials from its startup, and that broke every catalog lookup. Frontend, recommendation, and the LLM product-review tool all failed because of it.\n\n**Fix:** I ran `kubectl rollout restart deploy/product-catalog -n astronomy-shop`. The new pod read the current secret, and auth failures dropped to zero.\n\n**Verification:** Over about a minute after the restart, Postgres, frontend, and recommendation logs showed no auth errors, and every pod was Running.\n\nI did not change any manifests or secrets. The `product-catalog` deployment's `credential-source-pod-uid` annotation and the hardcoded credentials in the `accounting` and `product-reviews` specs are worth a follow-up review."}}
